# Repo-wide clangd settings. Directory .clangd files add to this rather than
# replace it - clangd reads every one from the file's directory up to the root
# and merges them - so the compilation databases stay where they are and the
# check list lives here once.
#
# WHY THE CHECK LIST HAS TO EXIST. clang-tidy is already enabled in clangd 18;
# the --clang-tidy flag makes no difference and passing it changes nothing.
# What decides whether anything runs is this list, and with no list clangd runs
# NO checks and reports nothing. Measured over the actual protocol, because
# `clangd --check` does not run clang-tidy at all and will tell you the file is
# clean however this is written.

Diagnostics:
  ClangTidy:
    Add:
      # The family that catches real defects rather than taste. This is where
      # the narrowing conversion lives that turned an Int32 pin number into an
      # Int64 and back on the way to gpio::open.
      - bugprone-*
      - clang-analyzer-*
      - performance-*
      - portability-*

      # Named individually rather than modernize-*, which would also demand
      # trailing return types and ban the C arrays firmware uses on purpose.
      # These four agree with docs/conventions.md instead of arguing with it.
      - modernize-use-nullptr
      - modernize-use-override
      - modernize-use-using
      - modernize-loop-convert

      # The braces rule, enforced where it is written rather than only in the
      # style audit - conventions.md requires a body to have braces however
      # short, and this is the check that says so as you type.
      - readability-braces-around-statements

    Remove:
      # Fires on any function with two parameters of the same type, which here
      # means most of the geometry and every begin/end pair. It is a real
      # hazard and an unreadable amount of noise; the ones that matter are
      # caught by reading the call site.
      - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters

      # The firmware is freestanding: no exceptions, no heap. A check that
      # wants RAII wrappers around a GPIO register has nothing to offer it.
      - bugprone-unhandled-exception-at-new
